  "lean": {
    "statement": "{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]\n    [CompleteSpace E] [SecondCountableTopology E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure E} [ProbabilityTheory.IsGaussian μ]\n    {L : ℝ≥0} {f : E → ℝ} (hf : LipschitzWith L f) :\n    MeasureTheory.Integrable f μ ∧ ∀ t : ℝ,\n      MeasureTheory.Integrable\n        (fun x => Real.exp (t * (f x - ∫ z, f z ∂μ))) μ",
    "statement_sha256": "386f8e0c54839adabeae5d0334fec161335e5940f61599a6df71831f8282002a",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "IsGaussian mu is the actual Mathlib Gaussian probability measure class: every real continuous linear functional has Gaussian pushforward. Mean need not be zero; the law may be degenerate.",
      "LipschitzWith L f is the actual global metric Lipschitz bound with nonnegative NNReal constant L, allowed to be zero. E is a complete second-countable real normed vector space with its Borel measurable structure.",
      "Integrable means Bochner integrability of the actual real-valued function under the actual measure. The integral in the exponential is that same function own mean. The quantified real t has both signs. No moment/MGF constant is supplied as data."
    ]
  },
